<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3, h4 { font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial; }
  .header-bar { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .title-section { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .title-section h1 { font-size: 48pt; margin: 0; line-height: 1.1; }
  .sponsored-by { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 50px; }
  .sponsored-by p { font-size: 12pt; margin: 5px 0; }
  .image-container { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 50px; }
  .image-container img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .section-header { font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 30px; text-align: center; }
  .event-schedule { display: flex; justify-content: space-around; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 50px; }
  .event-time, .event-activity { font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .event-details { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .event-details div { flex: 1; padding: 0 20px; }
  .program-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .program-list li { margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 12pt; }
  .program-list span { display: inline-block; width: 150px; font-weight: bold; }
  .content-section { margin-bottom: 50px; }
  .content-section h2 { font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 2px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 5px; }
  .content-section p { font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 15px; }
  .department-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .department-header h1 { font-size: 32pt; margin: 0; }
  .department-header p { font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 5px; }
  .department-details { margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .department-details h3 { font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold; }
  .department-details p { font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.5; }
  .footer-page-number { text-align: center; font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 50px; }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-bar">
    <div><span data-field="event_location">{{ event_location }}</span></div>
    <div><span data-field="event_date">{{ event_date }}</span></div>
    <div><div>JOIN BY ZOOM</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="title-section">
    <h1>Celebration of<br>Assessment Excellence</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="sponsored-by">
    <p>SPONSORED BY</p>
    <p>The Office of Assessment of Teaching & Learning</p>
    <p>Division of Academic Engagement & Student Achievement</p>
  </div>
  <div class="image-container">
    <img src="placeholder_image_1.jpg" alt="Event Image">
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="image-container">
    <img src="placeholder_image_2.jpg" alt="Activity Image">
    <div style="text-align: right; margin-top: 10px;"><span data-field="photographer_name">{{ photographer_name }}</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="footer-page-number">2</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-header">Order of Events</div>
  <div class="event-schedule">
    <div class="event-time">3:45 p</div>
    <div class="event-activity">Refreshments</div>
  </div>
  <div class="event-schedule">
    <div class="event-time">4:00 p</div>
    <div class="event-activity">Program</div>
  </div>
  <div class="event-details">
    <div>
      <strong>Opening Remarks</strong>
      <p><span data-field="speaker_name_1">{{ speaker_name_1 }}</span>, Interim Provost</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Recognition of Programs</strong>
      <p><span data-field="speaker_name_2">{{ speaker_name_2 }}</span>, Vice Provost for Academic Engagement & Student Achievement</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ul class="program-list">
    {% for dept in departments %}
    <li>
      <span>{{ dept.code }}:</span> {{ dept.name }}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <div class="footer-page-number">3</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="image-container">
    <img src="placeholder_image_3.jpg" alt="Classroom Image">
    <div style="text-align: right; margin-top: 10px;"><span data-field="photographer_name_2">{{ photographer_name_2 }}</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="footer-page-number">4</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>Assessment Philosophy</h2>
    <p>Effective assessment supports quality academic programs and advances <span data-field="university_name">{{ university_name }}</span>'s land grant mission and goals of providing a transformative student experience.</p>
    <p>Today, we celebrate and showcase good practices in assessment of learning outcomes by WSU's undergraduate programs.</p>
    <p>Over the past two years, these undergraduate degree programs, as appropriate to their context, have collected <span data-field="assessment_data_type">{{ assessment_data_type }}</span>, engaged faculty in discussions of assessment data, and used assessment results to improve curriculum or instruction.</p>
    <p>Examples provided highlight specific uses of program-level assessment by each program but are not comprehensive of all of the program's assessment activities or uses of assessment. We encourage faculty to share stories about how assessment evidence has helped inform improvements to their program and the learning experience of their students.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="footer-page-number">5</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="department-header">
    <p>Carson College of Business</p>
    <h1>Business Administration</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="department-details">
    <p>Assessment Leadership: <span data-field="assessment_leader_name">{{ assessment_leader_name }}</span>, Director of Assessment—Carson College of Business</p>
    <h3>Student Learning Outcome (SLO)</h3>
    <p>Demonstrate professional, socially responsible, and ethical awareness</p>
    <h3>Assessment of Student Learning</h3>
    <p>Business Administration collected performance data from their end of program exam and rubric scores for senior capstone essays. The program found some components of case analysis skills used for this learning outcome that could be strengthened.</p>
    <h3>Impact on Curriculum and/or Instruction</h3>
    <p>Based on these findings, program learning outcomes were revised to clarify skills for socially responsible and ethical awareness, focusing on changes to instruction, assignments, and assessment, and a 100-level course added to introduce case analysis skills.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="footer-page-number">6</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="department-header">
    <p>College of Agricultural, Human, and Natural Resource Sciences</p>
    <h1>Economic Sciences</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="department-details">
    <p>Assessment Leadership: <span data-field="assessment_leader_name_2">{{ assessment_leader_name_2 }}</span>, Current Director—School of Economic Sciences</p>
    <p>Assessment Leadership: <span data-field="assessment_leader_name_3">{{ assessment_leader_name_3 }}</span>, Past Director—School of Economic Sciences</p>
    <p>Assessment Leadership: <span data-field="assessment_leader_name_4">{{ assessment_leader_name_4 }}</span>, Assessment Coordinator</p>
    <h3>Student Learning Outcome (SLO)</h3>
    <p>Evaluate and apply economic concepts and quantitative methods</p>
    <h3>Assessment of Student Learning</h3>
    <p>Faculty reviewed internship mentor evaluations of student performance, along with senior exit interviews and course-specific measures for core courses. The program found that students needed more preparation in the areas of mathematical modeling and economic analysis using graphs and numerical methods.</p>
    <h3>Impact on Curriculum and/or Instruction</h3>
    <p>Based on this assessment, faculty developed a new 200-level course in applied economic modeling to better prepare students for upper-division work.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="footer-page-number">7</div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="department-header">
    <p>College of Arts and Sciences</p>
    <h1>Chemistry</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="department-details">
    <p>Assessment Leadership: <span data-field="assessment_leader_name_5">{{ assessment_leader_name_5 }}</span>, Department Chair</p>
    <p>Assessment Leadership: <span data-field="assessment_leader_name_6">{{ assessment_leader_name_6 }}</span>, Assessment Coordinator</p>
    <h3>Student Learning Outcome (SLO)</h3>
    <p>Communicate effectively about chemistry in writing</p>
    <h3>Assessment of Student Learning</h3>
    <p>Written assignments in the capstone course provided evidence of student writing skills, as seniors prepared for research poster presentations. Faculty found that students needed to improve how they structured their writing to communicate to a lay audience and make better use of editing and collaboration tools.</p>
    <h3>Impact on Curriculum and/or Instruction</h3>
    <p>Based on this assessment, changes were made to the capstone course design and assignments to include more collaborative writing tools, and additional short diagnostic assignments early in the semester.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="footer-page-number">8</div>
</div>

